{{!
    @template mod_interactivevideo/player/outcomelist

    The activity's learning outcomes and the learner's standing on each.

    Shown on the start and end screens of an interactive video or a flexbook when the
    teacher has switched the matching setting on. Re-rendered in place after the learner
    saves progress, so the wrapper keeps a stable data-region hook.

    Context variables required for this template:
    * outcomes - array of rows, each with:
      * name - the outcome's name
      * shortname - its short name, shown in brackets
      * rating - the learner's level on it, or the "No outcome" label
      * notrated - whether the learner has no rating yet

    Example context (json):
    {
        "outcomes": [
            {"name": "Describes the stages of the water cycle", "shortname": "WC-1",
                "rating": "Competent", "notrated": false},
            {"name": "Interprets a precipitation chart", "shortname": "WC-2",
                "rating": "No outcome", "notrated": true}
        ]
    }
}}
<div class="iv-outcome-list p-2 p-md-3" data-region="outcomelist">
    <h3 class="h5 iv-outcome-list-title d-flex align-items-center mb-2">
        <i class="bi bi-list-check iv-mr-2" aria-hidden="true"></i>{{#str}}outcomes, grades{{/str}}
    </h3>
    <ul class="list-group" aria-label="{{#str}}outcomes, grades{{/str}}">
        {{#outcomes}}
        <li class="list-group-item d-flex flex-wrap align-items-center justify-content-between">
            <span class="iv-outcome-list-name iv-mr-2">
                {{name}}{{#shortname}} <span class="text-muted">({{shortname}})</span>{{/shortname}}
            </span>
            <span class="badge iv-rounded-pill {{#notrated}}bg-secondary{{/notrated}}{{^notrated}}bg-success{{/notrated}}">
                {{rating}}
            </span>
        </li>
        {{/outcomes}}
    </ul>
</div>
